nimal reproduction. Exact concurrency at each failure, network/proxy conditions, and runtime version for each event have not been established. The OS build listed by the original issue author should not be assumed to describe this independent machine.\n\n#### Selected evidence\n\nRead-only inspection of local desktop logs found these selected occurrences (UTC):\n\nTimestamp  | Context  | Recorded package version\n\n#### Expected behavior and requested investigation\n\nTemporary discovery failures should recover within the running app where possible, or surface actionable guidance while preserving saved work and accurately reporting incomplete execution. Resuming a chat should not silently duplicate previously completed external writes.\n\nPlease investigate recovery of routing discovery during already-authenticated, ongoing work, and provide a supported workaround that preserves bundled-app features and does not require repeatedly restarting interrupted chats.\n\nIt would help to know which supported diagnostic capture can distinguish endpoint/network delays from internal routing/configuration waits, and whether a particular release contains a fix. No controlled restart, proxy change, runtime override, or clean-profile experiment was performed as part of this report.\n\n#### Privacy\n\nOnly selected diagnostic fields are included. No raw logs, source/book content, project details, local paths, credentials, account identifiers, session identifiers, or attachments are published.\n\nAdditional occurrence on November 3, 2026 — Windows desktop app 26.1027.3384.0 (Windows x64).\n\nObserved workflow: starting a new subagent failed twice with `Agent errored: workspace routing discovery timed out`, while follow-up tasks to existing subagents continued working. A later diagnostic subagent started successfully. This is intermittent; no deterministic minimal reproduction or concurrency-limit cause has been established.\n\nA bounded, read-only diagnostic of the local technical log database found at least 50 rows containing the exact timeout text between 2026-11-03 13:34:00 and 14:00:03 UTC:\n\n     * component: `codex_core::responses_retry`\n     * level: `WARN`\n     * `sampling_error=workspace routing discovery timed out`\n     * retry sequences: `retries=1..5`, `max_retries=5`\n     * example sequence timestamps (UTC): 13:34:00, 13:34:15, 13:34:30, 13:34:46, 13:35:03.\n\nThese are matching log rows, NOT fifty distinct failed subagents. The SQLite main database was read in immutable read-only mode, so recent WAL-only writes may be omitted.\n\nA separate issue appears in the desktop logs: activation of runtime update 26.1026.10807 repeatedly fails with `EPERM` while renaming the runtime cache directory, `failureStage=activate_runtime`, `hasConfiguredRuntime=true`. One observed timestamp is 2026-11-03 13:27:45.960 UTC. A causal relationship with the routing timeout is NOT established.\n\nThe root cause remains undetermined. No configuration changes, cache deletion, or application restart were performed during diagnosis. Please investigate the workspace-routing discovery/retry path and whether failed runtime activation contributes.\n\nOnly sanitized technical findings are shared here; no credentials, account identifiers, local username/path, raw log files, or conversation contents are attached.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nlimd-build-macos.sh · GitHub (https://gist.github.com/Bios597407/b244f612c5521ef4b74e55f5b32de5a6)\nciteturn7search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.8 years ago; Crawled: last month; If that's not what you want, run: unset PREFIX${NORMAL}\" ...  | echo -e \"${BOLD}PREFIX:${NORMAL} ${GREEN}$PREFIX${NORMAL}\"\n\n# Bios597407/limd-build-macos.sh\n\nForked from nikias/limd-build-macos.sh\n\nCreated January 6, 2021 10:59\n\nlimd-build-macos.sh\n\n | #!/bin/bash\n | \n | REV=1.0.4\n | \n | if test -x \"`which tput`\"; then\n | ncolors=`tput colors`\n | if test -n \"$ncolors\" &